==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
*{{l|ang|freġnan}}, {{l|ang|frīnan}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*fregnaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*preḱ-||to ask}}.

Cognate with Old Saxon {{m|osx|fregnan}}, Old Norse {{m|non|fregna}}, Gothic {{term|𐍆𐍂𐌰𐌹𐌷𐌽𐌰𐌽|tr=fraihnan|lang=got}}, and related to Old High German {{m|goh|frāga}} (German {{m|de|Frage}}).  The Indo-European root also gave Old Persian {{m|peo|||tr=aparsam|I asked}}, Irish {{m|ga|arco}}, Welsh {{m|cy|archaf}}, Old Armenian {{term|հարց||tr=harcʿ|lang=xcl}}, Tocharian A {{term|prak-|lang=xto}}, Tocharian B {{term|prek-|lang=txb}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈfrijnɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|head=friġnan}}

# to [[ask]], [[pray]]

